issing something, but I'd expect a deprecation warning if removing this method was planned.\r\n\r\nDetected when updating SQLAlchemy in Ibis: https://github.com/ibis-project/ibis/issues/2689\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nExpecting this same behaviour in 1.4:\r\n\r\n```py\r\n>>> import sqlalchemy\r\n>>> sqlalchemy.__version__\r\n'1.3.23'\r\n>>> sqlalchemy.table('my_table').columns.items()\r\n[]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\n```py\r\n>>> import sqlalchemy\r\n>>> sqlalchemy.__version__\r\n'1.4.0'\r\n>>> sqlalchemy.table('my_table').columns.items()\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Error**\r\n\r\n```\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/mgarcia/miniconda3/envs/ibis-dev/lib/python3.9/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1150, in __getattr__\r\n    return self._index[key]\r\nKeyError: 'items'\r\n\r\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\r\n\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n  File \"/home/mgarcia/miniconda3/envs/ibis-dev/lib/python3.9/site-packages/sqlalchemy/sql/base.py\", line 1152, in __getattr__\r\n    util.raise_(AttributeError(key), replace_context=err)\r\n  File \"/home/mgarcia/miniconda3/envs/ibis-dev/lib/python3.9/site-packages/sqlalchemy/util/compat.py\", line 198, in raise_\r\n    raise exception\r\nAttributeError: items\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Versions.**\r\n - OS: Linux\r\n - Python: Python 3.9.1 | packaged by conda-forge | (default, Jan 26 2021, 01:34:10)\r\n - SQLAlchemy: 1.4\r\n - Database:\r\n - DBAPI:\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/